This means that the Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to the evidence:
(i) whether the disablement is permanent or temporary;
(ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is permanent total disablement or permanent partial disablement;
(iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with reference to any MACT No.
147/2019 Suraj Kumar v. Arvind Kumar Page No. 8/18 BK specific limb, then the effect of such disablement of the limb on the functioning of the entire body,that is,
the permanent disability suffered by the person.
